        "depthCm": null,
        "weightKg": null
      },
      "description": "The rickroll: a link that promises one thing and delivers Rick Astley's 1987 video for \"Never Gonna Give You Up\". It began on 4chan in May 2007 as a twist on an older duck-themed prank, spread through the whole internet within a year, and has never gone away. The video itself was shot in London by Simon West and became, through the prank, one of the most-watched clips on YouTube. Shown here at the size of a 110-inch screen, frozen until you come close.",
      "facts": [
        "On 1 April 2008 YouTube rickrolled its own front page: every featured video linked to this one.",
        "Rick Astley himself rickrolled the 2008 Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade, popping out of a float mid-song.",
        "The video's YouTube id, dQw4w9WgXcQ, is recognised on sight by enough people that it is a meme in its own right.",
        "The still and the loop are shown under fair use; the video and song remain the property of their owners."
      ],
